ests":true,"pull_request_creation_policy":"all","topics":["airflow","apache","apache-airflow","automation","dag","data-engineering","data-integration","data-orchestrator","data-pipelines","data-science","elt","etl","machine-learning","mlops","orchestration","python","scheduler","workflow","workflow-engine","workflow-orchestration"],"visibility":"public","forks":18214,"open_issues":1927,"watchers":47308,"default_branch":"main","permissions":{"admin":false,"maintain":false,"push":false,"triage":false,"pull":true}},"pull_request":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/airflow/pulls/73805","html_url":"https://github.com/apache/airflow/pull/73805","diff_url":"https://github.com/apache/airflow/pull/73805.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/apache/airflow/pull/73805.patch","merged_at":"2026-10-05T17:28:41Z"},"body":"closes: #73803\n\nStacked on #72862 — that PR's commit is included in this branch's diff; only the second commit belongs to this change.\n\n## Why\n\n#72862 scopes `GET /ui/next_run_assets/{dag_id}` so `events` carries only the assets the caller may read, while `asset_expression` keeps a hidden slot for each unreadable one (#72864). `AssetSchedule.tsx` still derives both the total and its layout from `events`, so the Dag renders differently depending on who is looking at it.\n\nFor a Dag scheduled on assets A, B and C, a caller who may read only A sees:\n\n- \"0 of 1\" instead of \"0 of 3\" — `scheduledTotal` is `nextRunEvents.length`.\n- The single-asset layout instead of the popover, from the `nextRunEvents.length === 1` branch.\n- No asset schedule at all if none are readable — the `!nextRunEvents.length` branch falls back to `timetableSummary`, hiding that the Dag is asset triggered.\n\nThe popover contents are already correct: `AssetExpression` renders the hidden slots.\n\n## What\n\n- `NextRunAssetsResponse` gains `scheduling_asset_count`: how many assets the Dag is scheduled on, counted before the readable filter narrows the query. It reveals nothing new — the redacted expression already carries one slot per asset.\n- `AssetSchedule.tsx` uses it for `scheduledTotal` and for the two length-based branches. `scheduledCount` is unchanged: only readable, satisfied assets count as ready.\n\nThe count costs one extra query on an endpoint that renders once per Dag card, so `assert_queries_count` goes from 5 to 6. An alternative that avoids it — filtering unreadable rows in Python instead of SQL, taking the total from the unfiltered row count — would mean reworking #72862's approach; happy to switch if reviewers prefer that trade.\n\n---\n\n##### Was generative AI tooling used to co-author this PR?\n\n- [X] Yes — Claude Code (Claude Opus 5)\n","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/airflow/issues/73805/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/airflow/issues/73805/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null}},"event":"cross-referenced"},{"id":32275821209,"node_id":"LE_lADOAgUK288AAAABTgdjEc8AAAAHg8nymQ","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/airflow/issues/events/32275821209","actor":{"login":"bbovenzi","id":4600967,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ2MDA5Njc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4600967?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/bbovenzi","html_url":"https://github.com/bbovenzi","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bbovenzi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bbovenzi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bbovenzi/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bbovenzi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bbovenzi/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bbovenzi/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bbovenzi/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bbovenzi/events{/privacy}","r